Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x) = e^{2x}$ and $v(x)=\artanh{x}.$ So, we apply the product rule:

$$
 egin{aligned}{w}^{′}(x) & ={({e}^{2x})}^{′}\cdot 	ext{\artanh}x+{e}^{2x}\cdot {(	ext{\artanh}x)}^{′} \  & =2{e}^{2x}\cdot 	ext{\artanh}x+{e}^{2x}\cdot  rac{1}{1-{x}^{2}} \  & =2{e}^{2x}	ext{\artanh}x+{{ rac{{e}^{2x}}{1-{x}^{2}}}_{⏟}}_{y(x)}\end{aligned}
$$

Therefore, $y(x) = \dfrac{e^{2x}}{1 - x^2}.$
